faq:
  - q: Can we define our own delivery stages?
    a: Yes. An administrator builds the stages, the items in each stage and the documents required. Every job is then measured against that checklist.
  - q: Does it include utility and subsidy steps?
    a: Yes. Utility application, sanction, net metering and subsidy stages can be part of your checklist. They appear only on jobs where they apply, based on switches for subsidy, bank loan and utility approval.
  - q: Who can change a stage once it is assigned?
    a: The assigned person works the stage. Other users see it read-only unless their role holds an override permission, which is usually given to managers.
  - q: How are documents verified?
    a: A document is uploaded to the job and set to pending. The responsible person then marks it verified or rejected, and the status shows on the checklist.
  - q: Can we create agreements and letters from templates?
    a: Yes. Document templates produce PDF and Word documents filled with the details of the customer and project.
